        "title": {
          "fr": "Rotation des jetons de rafraîchissement avec détection de réutilisation",
          "en": "Refresh token rotation with reuse detection"
        },
        "file": "refresh_rotation.py",
        "lang": "python",
        "kind": "secure",
        "code": "import hashlib\nimport secrets\n\n# Refresh tokens are opaque random strings; the server stores only their hash.\n# hash -> {\"user\", \"family\", \"used\"}   (a database table in production)\nREFRESH_TOKENS = {}\nREVOKED_FAMILIES = set()\n\n\ndef digest(token):\n    # SHA-256 is fine here: the token has 256 bits of entropy, unlike a password\n    return hashlib.sha256(token.encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef issue(user, family=None):\n    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n    family = family or secrets.token_hex(8)\n    REFRESH_TOKENS[digest(token)] = {\"user\": user, \"family\": family, \"used\": False}\n    return token\n\n\ndef rotate(token):\n    \"\"\"Exchange a refresh token for a new one. Each token works exactly once.\"\"\"\n    record = REFRESH_TOKENS.get(digest(token))\n    if record is None or record[\"family\"] in REVOKED_FAMILIES:\n        raise PermissionError(\"invalid refresh token\")\n    if record[\"used\"]:\n        # Reuse means the token was stolen or replayed: revoke the whole family\n        REVOKED_FAMILIES.add(record[\"family\"])\n        raise PermissionError(\"reuse detected, session revoked\")\n    record[\"used\"] = True\n    # The new token stays in the same family so that theft can be traced\n    return issue(record[\"user\"], record[\"family\"])\n\n\ndef attempt(label, token):\n    try:\n        new_token = rotate(token)\n        print(f\"{label:28}: OK, new refresh token issued\")\n        return new_token\n    except PermissionError as error:\n        print(f\"{label:28}: DENIED ({error})\")\n        return None\n\n\nrt1 = issue(\"alice\")                      # login\nrt2 = attempt(\"alice rotates rt1\", rt1)   # normal use, 15 minutes later\nattempt(\"attacker replays stolen rt1\", rt1)\nattempt(\"alice uses rt2\", rt2)            # family revoked: alice must log in again\n",
        "output": "alice rotates rt1           : OK, new refresh token issued\nattacker replays stolen rt1 : DENIED (reuse detected, session revoked)\nalice uses rt2              : DENIED (invalid refresh token)\n",
        "note": {
          "fr": "Chaque jeton de rafraîchissement ne sert qu'une fois. Quand le jeton volé `rt1` est rejoué, le serveur ne peut pas savoir qui est le voleur : il révoque toute la famille, et Alice doit se reconnecter. C'est ce mécanisme qui rend la révocation possible malgré des jetons d'accès sans état.",
          "en": "Each refresh token works only once. When the stolen `rt1` is replayed, the server cannot tell who the thief is: it revokes the whole family, and Alice must log in again. This mechanism is what makes revocation possible despite stateless access tokens."
        }
